          .three-column-layout {\n                grid-template-columns: 1fr;\n            }\n\n            .technical-insights {\n                grid-column: 1;\n            }\n\n            .header-title {\n                font-size: 16px;\n            }\n\n            .header-nav {\n                display: none;\n            }\n        }\n\n        @media print {\n            body {\n                background-color: #ffffff;\n            }\n\n            .content-card {\n                break-inside: avoid;\n                page-break-inside: avoid;\n            }\n\n            header {\n                background-color: #ffffff;\n                border-bottom: 2px solid #000000;\n            }\n        }\n    </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n    <header>\n        <div class=\"container\">\n            <div class=\"header-title\">Agentic Coding Research Report</div>\n            <div class=\"header-date\">June 12, 2026</div>\n            <nav class=\"header-nav\">\n                <a href=\"#new-products\">New Products</a>\n                <a href=\"#whitelist-updates\">Updates</a>\n                <a href=\"#technical-insights\">Insights</a>\n            </nav>\n        </div>\n    </header>\n\n    <div class=\"sub-header\">\n        <div class=\"container\">\n            <span>Daily research report on agentic coding tools, updates, and insights</span>\n            <span>Updated: 2026-06-12</span>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <main>\n        <div class=\"container\">\n            <div class=\"three-column-layout\">\n                <!-- New Products Section (40%) -->\n                <section class=\"new-products\" id=\"new-products\">\n                    <div class=\"column-header\">New Products</div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-card\">\n                        <div class=\"card-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://github.com/OpenYabby/OpenYabby\" target=\"_blank\">OpenYabby</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"card-description\">\n                            An open-source voice-driven multi-agent orchestration system for AI coding workflows. Integrates with Claude Code and other CLI runners to enable project-scale development through coordinated agents.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"card-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"meta-tag\">Multi-agent orchestration</span>\n                            <span class=\"meta-date\">Released: 2026-06-09</span>\n                            <span class=\"meta-source\">Show HN, GitHub</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"community-quote\">\n                            \"Voice-driven multi-agent assistant for real project building on Mac. Runner-agnostic: supports Claude Code, Codex, Aider, Goose, Cline, and Continue\"\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                </section>\n\n                <!-- Whitelist Updates Section (35%) -->\n                <section class=\"whitelist-updates\" id=\"whitelist-updates\">\n                    <div class=\"column-header\">Product Updates</div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-card\">\n                        <div class=\"update-badge badge-feature\">Feature</div>\n                        <div class=\"card-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://windsurf.com/blog/changelist-jun25\" target=\"_blank\">Windsurf - Planning Mode & The Browser</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"card-description\">\n                            Windsurf introduced Planning Mode for collaborating with Cascade on long-term goals with persistent plan.md files, and The Browser with native AI integration and deep flow awareness.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"card-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2025-06-01</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"community-quote\">\n                            \"Super happy with planning mode. Being able to one shot tasks far more often than without planning mode.\"\n                            <span class=\"community-quote-source sentiment-positive\">Reddit - Positive</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"community-quote\">\n                            \"Planning mode takes 60+ seconds to update a single sentence\"\n                            <span class=\"community-quote-source sentiment-negative\">Reddit - Negative</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-card\">\n                        <div class=\"update-badge badge-release\">Release</div>\n                        <div class=\"card-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2025-07-15-github-copilot-in-vs-code-june-release-v1-102/\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub Copilot - VS Code June Release v1.102</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"card-description\">\n                            June 2025 release includes GitHub Copilot updates with Model Context Protocol (MCP) features becoming available and various improvements to the Copilot experience.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"card-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2025-06-01</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-card\">\n                        <div class=\"update-badge badge-release\">Release</div>\n                        <div class=\"card-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog/1-0\" target=\"_blank\">Cursor 1.0 - BugBot, Background Agent & One-Click MCP</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"card-description\">\n                            Cursor's first stable major release. Features include BugBot for automatic code review and bug fixing, Background Agent, Memories feature, One-Click MCP setup with OAuth support, and deep Jupyter Notebook integration.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"card-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2025-06-04</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"community-quote\">\n                            \"Cursor reached $100 million ARR in June 2025, making it one of the fastest software products to achieve this milestone\"\n                            <span class=\"community-quote-source sentiment-positive\">Industry news - Positive</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-card\">\n                        <div class=\"update-badge badge-feature\">Feature</div>\n                        <div class=\"card-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://changelog.continue.dev/\" target=\"_blank\">Continue - Enhanced MCP Support</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"card-description\">\n                            v1.0.12 for VS Code and v1.0.21 for JetBrains with enhanced Model Context Protocol (MCP) support including SSE and Streamable HTTP transports for remote hosting.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"card-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2025-06-13</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-card\">\n                        <div class=\"update-badge badge-release\">Release</div>\n                        <div class=\"card-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://medium.com/data-and-beyond/rewriting-the-command-line-how-google-gemini-cli-is-turning-terminals-into-ai-powered-super-tools-01d95161bc59\" target=\"_blank\">Gemini CLI - Open-Source AI for Terminals</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"card-description\">\n                            Google launched Gemini CLI as an open-source command-line interface that brings Gemini AI capabilities directly into terminal environments.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"card-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2025-06-25</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"community-quote\">\n                            \"Gemini CLI 'changes everything for developers' - turning terminals into 'AI-powered super tools'\"\n                            <span class=\"community-quote-source sentiment-positive\">Medium - Positive</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-card\">\n                        <div class=\"update-badge badge-release\">Release</div>\n                        <div class=\"card-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://github.com/Aider-AI/aider/releases\" target=\"_blank\">Aider v0.85.0 - Responses API Models & Gemini 2.5</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"card-description\">\n                            Support for Responses API models including o1-pro and o3-pro, new Gemini 2.5 Pro models support. Gemini 2.5 Pro achieved SOTA on the aider polyglot coding leaderboard with 73% score.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"card-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2025-06-27</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"community-quote\">\n                            \"Gemini 2.5 Pro set the SOTA (State of the Art) on the aider polyglot coding leaderboard with a score of 73%, well ahead of thinking/reasoning models\"\n                            <span class=\"community-quote-source sentiment-positive\">Reddit - Positive</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                </section>\n\n                <!-- Technical Insights Section (25%) -->\n                <section class=\"technical-insights\" id=\"technical-insights\">\n                    <div class=\"column-header\">Technical Insights</div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-card\">\n                        <div class=\"card-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/06/10/datadog-veterans-launch-ai-coding-startup-niteshift-on-a-bet-against-big-ai-lock-in/\" target=\"_blank\">Niteshift Raises $7M Seed</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"card-description\">\n                            Datadog veterans launched AI coding startup Niteshift with a $7 million seed round led by Greylock's Jerry Chen, betting against big AI lock-in.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"card-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"meta-source\">TechCrunch</span>\n                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2026-06-10</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div style=\"margin-top: 8px;\">\n                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">ai-coding</span>\n                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">startups</span>\n                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">developer-tools</span>\n                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">venture-capital</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-card\">\n                        <div class=\"card-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">OpenAI Launches Lockdown Mode</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"card-description\">\n                            OpenAI rolled out Lockdown Mode to help prevent data exfiltration from prompt injection attacks by limiting outbound network requests. Directly attacks the 'exfiltration vectors' leg of the Lethal Trifecta.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"card-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"meta-source\">Simon Willison</span>\n                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2026-06-05</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div style=\"margin-top: 8px;\">\n                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">security</span>\n                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">prompt-injection</span>\n                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">llms</span>\n                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">openai</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-card\">\n                        <div class=\"card-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">AI Enthusiasts vs Skeptics</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"card-description\">\n                            Charity Majors captures the dynamic: enthusiasts race against discontinuous capability leaps creating existential threats, while skeptics race against entropy as faster code shipping degrades reliability.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"card-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"meta-source\">Simon Willison (quoting Charity Majors)</span>\n                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2026-06-04</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div style=\"margin-top: 8px;\">\n                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">ai</span>\n                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">engineering</span>\n                            <span class=\"insight-topic\">organizational-design</span>\n                        </div