iv>\n                        <div class=\"community-quote\">\n                            \"Super happy with planning mode. Being able to one shot tasks far more often than without planning mode.\"\n                            <span class=\"community-quote-source sentiment-positive\">Reddit - Positive</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"community-quote\">\n                            \"Planning mode takes 60+ seconds to update a single sentence\"\n                            <span class=\"community-quote-source sentiment-negative\">Reddit - Negative</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-card\">\n                        <div class=\"update-badge badge-release\">Release</div>\n                        <div class=\"card-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2025-07-15-github-copilot-in-vs-code-june-release-v1-102/\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub Copilot - VS Code June Release v1.102</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"card-description\">\n                            June 2025 release includes GitHub Copilot updates with Model Context Protocol (MCP) features becoming available and various improvements to the Copilot experience.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"card-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2025-06-01</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-card\">\n                        <div class=\"update-badge badge-release\">Release</div>\n                        <div class=\"card-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog/1-0\" target=\"_blank\">Cursor 1.0 - BugBot, Background Agent & One-Click MCP</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"card-description\">\n                            Cursor's first stable major release. Features include BugBot for automatic code review and bug fixing, Background Agent, Memories feature, One-Click MCP setup with OAuth support, and deep Jupyter Notebook integration.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"card-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2025-06-04</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"community-quote\">\n                            \"Cursor reached $100 million ARR in June 2025, making it one of the fastest software products to achieve this milestone\"\n                            <span class=\"community-quote-source sentiment-positive\">Industry news - Positive</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-card\">\n                        <div class=\"update-badge badge-feature\">Feature</div>\n                        <div class=\"card-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://changelog.continue.dev/\" target=\"_blank\">Continue - Enhanced MCP Support</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"card-description\">\n                            v1.0.12 for VS Code and v1.0.21 for JetBrains with enhanced Model Context Protocol (MCP) support including SSE and Streamable HTTP transports for remote hosting.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"card-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2025-06-13</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-card\">\n                        <div class=\"update-badge badge-release\">Release</div>\n                        <div class=\"card-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://medium.com/data-and-beyond/rewriting-the-command-line-how-google-gemini-cli-is-turning-terminals-into-ai-powered-super-tools-01d95161bc59\" target=\"_blank\">Gemini CLI - Open-Source AI for Terminals</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"card-description\">\n                            Google launched Gemini CLI as an open-source command-line interface that brings Gemini AI capabilities directly into terminal environments.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"card-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2025-06-25</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"community-quote\">\n                            \"Gemini CLI 'changes everything for developers' - turning terminals into 'AI-powered super tools'\"\n                            <span class=\"community-quote-source sentiment-positive\">Medium - Positive</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"content-card\">\n                        <div class=\"update-badge badge-release\">Release</div>\n                        <div class=\"card-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://github.com/Aider-AI/aider/releases\" target=\"_blank\">Aider v0.85.0 - Responses API Models & Gemini 2.5</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"card-description\">\n                            Support for Responses API models including o1-pro and o3-pro, new Gemini 2.5 Pro models support. Gemini 2.5 Pro achieved SOTA on the aider polyglot coding leaderboard with 73% score.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"card-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2025-06-27</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"community-quote\">\n                            \"Gemini 2.5 Pro set the SOTA (State of the Art) on the aider polyglot coding leaderboard with a score of 73%, well ahead of thinking/reasoning models\"\n                            <span class=\"community-quote-source sentiment-positive\">